  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Calculate the theoretical a/b/c/x/y/z fragment ions of a modified peptide over a range of charges, then match them to a pasted MS/MS peak list within a Th or ppm tolerance, with an annotated spectrum, a sequence coverage table, Hyperscore/Binomial scores and CSV export. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
